<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_Process_KgSeparation" targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns#" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="administrator" name="Administrator"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="platform-authoring-agent" name="Platform authoring agent"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Process_KgSeparation">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Process_KgSeparation" name="A knowledge graph leaves for its own repositories" processRef="Process_KgSeparation"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_KgSeparation" name="A knowledge graph leaves for its own repositories" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Move part of a knowledge graph into repositories of its own: the content and the tools that write and check it separate as a pair, into two repositories, not one. The content (files to read, no code) and its tools (the code that writes and checks it) separate as a pair. `kg-separation.md` is the practice; this is its order and its gates. Stages 1-3 are `graph-detanglement`, reused rather than restated.

EVERY GATEWAY IS A COMMAND. `Tools closed?` is `check:tools-closure` with the content's no-code test and a byte-identity check on the generated files; `Every identifier its file's path?` is `check:node-iris`; `Green alone?` is the standalone rehearsal; `Ready to seed?` is `seed:ready --layer &lt;name&gt; --rehearse`, decided by decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn. A check that could not run stops the process rather than reading as clean.

A PERSON DECIDES FOUR TIMES, AND THE ADMINISTRATOR LANE SAYS WHERE: whether to separate at all, whether to authorise the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover. Nothing is committed to the new repositories before they are created, and the parent keeps its own copy until it consumes the first release.

VERSIONS: the pair starts at the content's version at the split, then each is versioned on its own; a tools release lists the content majors it supports. Worked example: bootstrap and bootstrap-tools (beans r3gy, xsqm). cat-harness and cat-harness-tools follow the same stages. DRAWN IN PHASES (owner, 2026-11-02, G5): each phase is its own diagram, called here, and the bean is opened and closed once at this level.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_Process_KgSeparation">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Authoring agent" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Briefs, measures the signals, runs declare-detangle-isolate, reports what would move, seeds the repositories once they exist, and adopts each later release. Verification is always by re-running a gate, never by a change looking right.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Trigger</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanOpen</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_BeanNotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Brief</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Measure</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Detangle</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_MeasuredOut</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Move</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Moved</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Platform" name="Platform authoring agent" partitionElementRef="platform-authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>The platform-side stages: the graph's identity (version, iriBase, nodeSchemas), moving harness output about it into the host, splitting the content from its tools, and making the parent consume the pair additively.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Prepare</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Prepared</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Admin" name="Administrator" partitionElementRef="administrator">
        <bpmn:documentation>The person's decisions: whether to separate at all, authorising the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover that retires the parent's copy. An agent reports and waits at each; none of them may be relaxed by a package.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Decide</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Separate</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Authorise</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Authorised</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Cutover</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_BeanClose</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BeanClosedHow</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Separated</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Declined</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Stays</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Unknown</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Trigger" name="Too large, or readers&#10;and cadence differ">
      <bpmn:outgoing>F0</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanOpen" name="Open the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanOpen">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F0</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanYours" name="Bean claimed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_BeanNotYours" name="Not yours —&#10;left alone">
      <bpmn:documentation>Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Brief" name="Brief the work" calledElement="GT_Brief">
      <bpmn:documentation>Here the work is a separation: what is separating, and why.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Measure" name="Measure the signals">
      <bpmn:documentation>Files and bytes per instance, clone cost (`bun run cat health`), gate time, merge contention, the candidate's cohesion and cut (`kg:detangle`), wrong-direction edges, and the would-be tools package's import cone. Recorded in the bean; none alone is a trigger.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:dataOutputAssociation id="DOA_Beans_Task_Measure">
        <bpmn:targetRef>DSR_beans_Task_Measure</bpmn:targetRef>
      </bpmn:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Decide" calledElement="Process_AskThePerson" name="Ask whether to&#10;separate it">
      <bpmn:documentation>The owner decides from the measured signals, and also decides the address base for its identifiers, where verdicts about it live, and what its tools repository owns. Declining is a real outcome: the graph stays where it is.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Separate" name="Separate this graph?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads the owner's answer to the ask before it. Declining is a real outcome: the graph stays where it is.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_Detangle" name="Declare, detangle&#10;and isolate it" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationDetangle">
      <bpmn:documentation>Stages 1-3, the graph-detanglement gates: declared in place, zero wrong-direction edges on every axis, and standing alone. A call to the shared phase, so graph-detanglement's own authorise-and-extract steps are not run twice.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="graph-detanglement"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_MeasuredOut" name="Measured out?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the detangle phase reached: isolated, or could not determine.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Prepare" name="Prepare it to&#10;stand alone" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationPrepare">
      <bpmn:documentation>Stages 4-8: identity, hosted output, the content-tools split, publication plan, and the standalone rehearsal.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Prepared" name="Green alone?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the prepare phase reached. An unseen edge sends the graph back to detangling: a loop that crosses phases is drawn here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F10</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F11</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Authorise" name="Authorise the&#10;extraction" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationAuthorise">
      <bpmn:documentation>Stage 9: report what moves and ask the administrator. A repository cut changes the substrate every other process binds to; that is a person's decision.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="deletion-requires-confirmation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Authorised" name="Authorised?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the authorise phase reached. Declining leaves the graph declared, detangled, isolated and split in place.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F14</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Move" name="Move it into its&#10;repositories" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationMove">
      <bpmn:documentation>Stages 10-12: create the repositories, drain, seed, consume additively, release, and check every identifier dereferences.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Moved" name="Seeded and&#10;released?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads which end the move phase reached. Nothing is seeded on an unknown readiness.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>F16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F17</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Cutover" name="Cut over" calledElement="Process_KgSeparationCutover">
      <bpmn:documentation>Stage 13: retire the parent's copy and measure the cutover until it is complete or cannot be shown complete.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="kg-separation"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_BeanClose" name="Close the bean" calledElement="Process_BeanClose">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BeanClosedHow" name="How did it end?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Which outcome the bean was closed with, so each ends at its own named end event. The bean is closed once, on every path (bpmn-authoring: open and close the bean at the top, once).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>SF_Bean_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Separated" name="Separated">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_5</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Declined" name="Stays in place,&#10;ready to leave">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Stays" name="Stays where it is">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Unknown" name="UNKNOWN — stop.&#10;Not clean">
      <bpmn:incoming>SF_Bean_8</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F0" sourceRef="Start_Trigger" targetRef="Call_BeanOpen"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_2" sourceRef="Call_BeanOpen" targetRef="GW_BeanYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_1" name="claimed" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="Task_Brief"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_3" name="not yours" sourceRef="GW_BeanYours" targetRef="End_BeanNotYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F1" sourceRef="Task_Brief" targetRef="Task_Measure"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F2" sourceRef="Task_Measure" targetRef="Task_Decide"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F3" sourceRef="Task_Decide" targetRef="GW_Separate"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F4" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_Separate" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F5" name="separate" sourceRef="GW_Separate" targetRef="Task_Detangle"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F6" sourceRef="Task_Detangle" targetRef="GW_MeasuredOut"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F7" name="isolated" sourceRef="GW_MeasuredOut" targetRef="Call_Prepare"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F8" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_MeasuredOut" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F9" sourceRef="Call_Prepare" targetRef="GW_Prepared"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F10" name="green" sourceRef="GW_Prepared" targetRef="Call_Authorise"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F11" name="red: an unseen edge" sourceRef="GW_Prepared" targetRef="Task_Detangle"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F12" name="could not run" sourceRef="GW_Prepared" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F13" sourceRef="Call_Authorise" targetRef="GW_Authorised"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F14" name="authorised" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="Call_Move"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F15" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_Authorised" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F16" sourceRef="Call_Move" targetRef="GW_Moved"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F17" name="released" sourceRef="GW_Moved" targetRef="Call_Cutover"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F18" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_Moved" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F19" sourceRef="Call_Cutover" targetRef="Call_BeanClose"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_4" sourceRef="Call_BeanClose" targetRef="GW_BeanClosedHow"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_5" name="separated" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Separated"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_6" name="declined" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Declined"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_7" name="stays" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Stays"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="SF_Bean_8" name="unknown" sourceRef="GW_BeanClosedHow" targetRef="End_Unknown"/>
    <bpmn:dataStoreReference id="DSR_beans_Task_Measure" name="Beans" dataStoreRef="work-plan"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Process_KgSeparation">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Process_KgSeparation" bpmnElement="Collaboration_Process_KgSeparation">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_Process_KgSeparation" bpmnElement="Participant_Process_KgSeparation" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="130" y="60" width="3605" height="1500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Agent" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="3575" height="500"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Platform" bpmnElement="Lane_Platform" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="560" width="3575" height="250"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Admin" bpmnElement="Lane_Admin" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="810" width="3575" height="750"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Trigger" bpmnElement="Start_Trigger"><dc:Bounds x="272" y="132" width="36" height="36"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="240" y="174" width="100" height="40"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_BeanOpen" bpmnElement="Call_BeanOpen"><dc:Bounds x="405" y="90" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_BeanYours" bpmnElement="GW_BeanYours"><dc:Bounds x="615" y="125" width="50" height="50"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="647" y="95" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_BeanNotYours" bpmnElement="End_BeanNotYours"><dc:Bounds x="622" y="382" width="36" height="36"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="590" y="424" width="100" height="40"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Brief" bpmnElement="Task_Brief"><dc:Bounds x="755" y="90" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Measure" bpmnElement="Task_Measure"><dc:Bounds x="930" y="90" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Decide" bpmnElement="Task_Decide"><dc:Bounds x="1105" y="840" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Separate" bpmnElement="GW_Separate"><dc:Bounds x="1315" y="875" width="50" height="50"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1290" y="835" width="100" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Task_Detangle" bpmnElement="Task_Detangle"><dc:Bounds x="1455" y="90" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_MeasuredOut" bpmnElement="GW_MeasuredOut"><dc:Bounds x="1665" y="125" width="50" height="50"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1697" y="95" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Prepare" bpmnElement="Call_Prepare"><dc:Bounds x="1805" y="590" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Prepared" bpmnElement="GW_Prepared"><dc:Bounds x="2015" y="625" width="50" height="50"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="2047" y="595" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Authorise" bpmnElement="Call_Authorise"><dc:Bounds x="2155" y="840" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Authorised" bpmnElement="GW_Authorised"><dc:Bounds x="2365" y="875" width="50" height="50"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="2340" y="854" width="100" height="17" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Call_Move" bpmnElement="Call_Move"><dc:Bounds x="2505" y="90" width="120" height="120"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
